Name: octave_libbpf
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-10-05
Author: Yu Hongbo
Maintainer: Yu Hongbo
Title: Write and run eBPF programs from GNU Octave
Description: octave_libbpf is a GNU Octave wrapper around libbpf, the reference
 userspace library for loading and interacting with eBPF programs.  It allows
 Octave m-code to open, verify, load, attach, pin and introspect eBPF objects,
 to read and write eBPF maps, to consume BPF ring buffers and perf buffers, and
 to inspect BTF type information.  On top of that low level binding it ships a
 pure m-code eBPF toolchain: an instruction encoder/assembler, a BTF type
 encoder and an ELF64/BPF object writer, so complete eBPF programs and their
 maps can be authored directly in Octave without a C compiler.  A small
 object-oriented layer (bpf.Object, bpf.Program, bpf.Map, bpf.Link, ...) makes
 the common workflows concise.
Categories: external-interfaces
Depends: octave (>= 8.0.0)
License: BSD-2-Clause
Url: https://github.com/CNOCTAVE/octave_libbpf
